WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.710
Yoghurt is milk that bacteria
have turned thick and sour,

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:04.770
on purpose.

3
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.290
But the air, your hands and the
surfaces around you carry other

4
00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.830
microbes too.

5
00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.530
Let the wrong ones in, and the
whole batch could be spoiled.

6
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.630
So how do food makers make sure
that only the microbes they

7
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.410
want can grow?

8
00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.770
In this mission, you'll find
out what yoghurt bacteria do to

9
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.030
the sugar in milk.

10
00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:27.350
You'll look inside an industrial
fermenter and see which

11
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.810
conditions are kept under control.

12
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:33.150
And you'll find out how fish
farmers get the most from their

13
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.930
tanks and cages.

14
00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:38.630
Your mission: explain how food
makers keep the wrong microbes

15
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:39.770
out.
